{#
  sync_list excludes everything by default -- only what is listed here is
  synchronised, and an exclusion always beats an inclusion.

  Rules are anchored with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored rule like
  `Books` instructs the client to scan every folder, online and local, looking
  for anything of that name, which is the most expensive form of rule there is.
-#}
# Managed by Ansible (roles/onedrive). Local edits will be overwritten.
#
# Rule reference: /usr/share/doc/onedrive/usage.md
# Account: {{ account.name }}
#
# Everything not listed below is excluded from synchronisation. Changing these
# rules only takes effect after a full resynchronisation:
#
#     setup-onedrive-{{ account.name }}.sh --resync
{% for rule in account.sync_list %}
{{ rule }}
{% endfor %}
